    "nci_treatment": "Flows are consolidated (incl. 40% outside stake in Turner & Townsend and other partly-owned subs). NCI charged once in the equity bridge at ~12x FY2025 NCI earnings (120 NCI + 26 redeemable NCI = 146) = -1,750, versus book 776 (322 NCI + 454 redeemable NCI).",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build, 10-year horizon. CBRE is a fee-earning commercial real estate SERVICES operating company (advisory/brokerage, facilities and project management, investment management) -- it does not own an IAS-40 property portfolio or distribute AFFO, so the REIT row does not apply; the cyclical-operating-company row of dcf-methods routes it to owner-FCF. Base EBITDA is GAAP operating income + D&A (FY2025 2,482 = 6.1%) plus SBC (120) = 6.4% pre-SBC, NOT management's Core EBITDA, which also adds back integration/carried-interest items. D&A (1.8% of revenue) is inflated by acquired-intangible amortization (393 in FY2025, scheduled 376/322/292/260/236) and is glided down toward ~1.1% as it rolls off. Acquisitions (FY2025 $1.37bn cash, incl. Pearce $1.2bn Nov-25) are NOT modelled: revenue growth paths are meant to be mostly organic plus the already-paid-for Pearce/Industrious contribution; a CBRE that keeps buying growth will out-grow these paths but at the cost of cash the model does not charge. Interest income not stripped (net debt company). Cash tax on unlevered EBIT ~23% (FY2025 GAAP ETR 19.9% on levered pretax; cash taxes 599). FY2025 equity-award taxes (37) backfilled to kpis via make fix. Q2-2026 10-Q is the latest filing; Q3 2026 results due late October.",
